---
{
  title: "bottom_n"
}
---
### NAME

    bottom_n() - The elements with the lowest scores, lowest first. Works
    like top_n(), ties included, from the other end.

### SYNOPSIS

    varargs mixed *bottom_n( mixed *arr, int n, mixed fn, int strict );

### DESCRIPTION

    The elements with the lowest scores, lowest first. Works like top_n(),
    ties included, from the other end.

### PARAMETERS

    arr     (mixed*)
            The elements to rank.

    n       (int)
            How many places to keep.

    fn      (function|int, optional)
            Returns each element's score; or strict, when an int.

    strict  (int, optional, default: 0)
            Whether to keep exactly n elements, when fn is a function.

### RETURN VALUES

    (mixed*) The kept elements, lowest score first.

### ERRORS

    If arr is not an array If n is not a non-negative integer If fn is not
    undefined, an integer or a function

### EXAMPLE

    {{di1}}bottom_n(({ 3, 1, 1, 2 }), 1);    // ({ 1, 1 })
    bottom_n(({ 3, 1, 1, 2 }), 1, 1); // ({ 1 }){{di0}}
